{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_tests_purchasing_test_purchasing_test", "label": "purchasing_test (card ^ref-19)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/tests/purchasing_test.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Failure-case suite for fn_create_po, fn_add_po_delivery and v_po_outstanding, TC-05 ... TC-19 and TC-21 ... TC-33 of TDD-purchasing.md. Asserts: an L2, an L3 or a deactivated Owner cannot raise a PO (ADR-004, R31); created_by and seq are not parameters; a retry books no second round, since every lot, freight share and yield figure downstream would inherit the double (R4); a genuine second identical round is not refused as if it were that retry; a round cannot be booked past the ordered weight; a round is never written without a lot, and the lot's weight is the round's (D01, R16) so BR03's loss base is a weight that actually moved; a lot is dispatched to the chef house, not a branch (BR11); the card posts nothing to stock_ledger, so meat is not in stock days before the truck; and no session SELECT is granted on a price-bearing table (ADR-004, R20). TC-20 needs two sessions and lives in purchasing_concurrency_test.sh."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_tests_purchasing_test_purchasing_test", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_create_po_fn_create_po", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/purchasing_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_purchasing_test_purchasing_test", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_add_po_delivery_fn_add_po_delivery", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/purchasing_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_purchasing_test_purchasing_test", "target": "supabase_views_030_v_po_outstanding_v_po_outstanding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EX